    <!-- ============ (e) fix patterns ============ -->
    <section class="section-tight" id="fixes">
      <div class="container">
        <h2 class="viz-h">
          <span class="lang-en">e · The published fix patterns</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">e · 공개된 fix 패턴들</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="viz-sub">
          <span class="lang-en">
            Each failure above has a published answer. Flip each card between the broken layout and
            the engineered one — every pattern is cited to the paper that documented it.
          </span><span class="lang-ko">
            위의 각 failure에는 공개된 답이 있다. 카드를 깨진 layout과 엔지니어링된 layout 사이로
            뒤집어 보라 — 모든 패턴은 그것을 기록한 논문을 인용한다.
          </span>
        </p>

        <div class="fix-grid">

          <!-- F-a pools -->
          <article class="fix-card">
            <span class="card-kicker">F-a · Atom → DiffKV · Any-Precision LLM</span>
            <h3><span class="lang-en">Precision-partitioned pools</span><span class="lang-ko">precision별 분할 pool</span></h3>
            <div class="ba-btns" role="group" aria-label="Before / after">
              <button class="ba-btn on" type="button" data-show="before"><span class="lang-en">broken</span><span class="lang-ko">깨진 상태</span></button>
              <button class="ba-btn" type="button" data-show="after"><span class="lang-en">fixed</span><span class="lang-ko">고친 상태</span></button>
            </div>
            <figure class="fix-fig fig-before on">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 420 96" class="fig-svg" role="img" aria-label="Interleaved mixed-width records">
                {[
                  { w: 34, b: '4b' }, { w: 18, b: '2b' }, { w: 96, b: '16b' }, { w: 60, b: '8b' },
                  { w: 34, b: '4b' }, { w: 18, b: '2b' }, { w: 60, b: '8b' }, { w: 34, b: '4b' },
                ].map((r, i, arr) => {
                  const x = 20 + arr.slice(0, i).reduce((a, c) => a + c.w + 4, 0);
                  return (
                    <g>
                      <rect x={x} y="26" width={r.w} height="28" rx="5" fill="var(--accent-soft)" stroke="var(--accent)"></rect>
                      <text x={x + r.w / 2} y="45" text-anchor="middle" class="t-mono t-tiny">{r.b}</text>
                    </g>
                  );
                })}
                <text x="20" y="80" class="t-tiny t-tert">interleaved widths: every warp hits every failure in section d</text>
              </svg>
              <figcaption><span class="lang-en">before — one stream, mixed records</span><span class="lang-ko">before — 한 stream에 혼합 record</span></figcaption>
            </figure>
            <figure class="fix-fig fig-after">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 420 96" class="fig-svg" role="img" aria-label="Per-width contiguous pools with a tag array">
                <rect x="20" y="20" width="180" height="34" rx="6" fill="var(--accent-soft)" stroke="var(--accent)"></rect>
                <text x="110" y="42" text-anchor="middle" class="t-mono t-tiny">4-bit pool · uniform tiles</text>
                <rect x="212" y="20" width="120" height="34" rx="6" fill="#e6e9df" stroke="var(--swatch-olive)"></rect>
                <text x="272" y="42" text-anchor="middle" class="t-mono t-tiny">8-bit pool</text>
                <rect x="344" y="20" width="56" height="34" rx="6" fill="#eaf1f8" stroke="var(--swatch-sky)"></rect>
                <text x="372" y="42" text-anchor="middle" class="t-mono t-tiny">tags</text>
                <text x="20" y="80" class="t-tiny t-tert">within a pool: affine addresses, one code path, aligned loads</text>
              </svg>
              <figcaption><span class="lang-en">after — per-width contiguous regions + uniform tiles</span><span class="lang-ko">after — width별 연속 영역 + uniform tile</span></figcaption>
            </figure>
            <p class="fix-cite">
              <span class="lang-en">
                Atom is the ancestor: it “reorders the scattered outlier channels … to the end of
                the matrix” so each region is uniform. DiffKV builds the KV-cache version —
                differentiated pages plus a GPU memory manager that “compacts fragmented free
                memory … in parallel” (2.7–5.7× compression, 1.9–5.4× throughput). Any-Precision
                LLM goes further with bitplanes: width becomes <em>which planes you read</em>, and
                lower width “directly translates into proportional speedup.”
              </span><span class="lang-ko">
                조상은 Atom이다: “흩어진 outlier channel을 행렬 끝으로 reorder”해 각 영역을
                uniform하게 만든다. DiffKV는 KV-cache 버전을 만든다 — differentiated page와
                “파편화된 free memory를 병렬로 compact하는” GPU memory manager (압축 2.7–5.7×,
                throughput 1.9–5.4×). Any-Precision LLM은 bitplane으로 더 나간다: width가
                <em>읽는 plane의 수</em>가 되고, 낮은 width는 “비례하는 speedup으로 직결된다.”
              </span>
            </p>
          </article>

          <!-- F-b fused dequant -->
          <article class="fix-card">
            <span class="card-kicker">F-b · KIVI · KVQuant · Atom</span>
            <h3><span class="lang-en">Fused dequant-in-registers</span><span class="lang-ko">register 안에서 fused dequant</span></h3>
            <div class="ba-btns" role="group" aria-label="Before / after">
              <button class="ba-btn on" type="button" data-show="before"><span class="lang-en">broken</span><span class="lang-ko">깨진 상태</span></button>
              <button class="ba-btn" type="button" data-show="after"><span class="lang-en">fixed</span><span class="lang-ko">고친 상태</span></button>
            </div>
            <figure class="fix-fig fig-before on">
              <div class="flow">
                <span class="fchip mem">HBM · packed</span><span class="farr">→</span>
                <span class="fchip warn">dequant kernel</span><span class="farr">→</span>
                <span class="fchip mem">HBM · fp16 buffer</span><span class="farr">→</span>
                <span class="fchip">GEMV</span>
              </div>
              <figcaption><span class="lang-en">before — dequantize to a DRAM buffer: the fp16 bytes you deleted get written and re-read</span><span class="lang-ko">before — DRAM buffer로 dequantize: 지웠던 fp16 byte를 다시 쓰고 다시 읽는다</span></figcaption>
            </figure>
            <figure class="fix-fig fig-after">
              <div class="flow">
                <span class="fchip mem">HBM · packed</span><span class="farr">→</span>
                <span class="fchip good">registers: unpack + dequant + FMA</span><span class="farr">→</span>
                <span class="fchip">output</span>
              </div>
              <figcaption><span class="lang-en">after — only low-bit values ever cross DRAM</span><span class="lang-ko">after — DRAM을 건너는 것은 low-bit 값뿐</span></figcaption>
            </figure>
            <p class="fix-cite">
              <span class="lang-en">
                KIVI: “We have fused the dequantization process with matrix multiplication.”
                KVQuant fuses 4-bit LUT dequant and on-the-fly RoPE into the matvec — Key matvec
                33.3 → 25.6 µs at 2K context — 1.2–1.6× (Key) / 1.3–1.7× (Value) <em>faster</em> than fp16. Atom “fuses
                dequantization with FlashInfer … so that only low-bit values from KV-cache are
                loaded.”
              </span><span class="lang-ko">
                KIVI: “dequantization을 matrix multiplication과 fuse했다.” KVQuant는 4-bit LUT
                dequant와 on-the-fly RoPE를 matvec에 fuse한다 — 2K context에서 Key matvec 33.3 →
                25.6 µs — fp16보다 1.2–1.6× (Key) / 1.3–1.7× (Value) <em>빠르다</em>. Atom은 “dequantization을 FlashInfer에
                fuse해 KV-cache에서 low-bit 값만 load되게” 한다.
              </span>
            </p>
          </article>

          <!-- F-c offline interleaving -->
          <article class="fix-card">
            <span class="card-kicker">F-c · MARLIN · QServe · FLUTE</span>
            <h3><span class="lang-en">Offline interleaved packing</span><span class="lang-ko">offline interleaved packing</span></h3>
            <div class="ba-btns" role="group" aria-label="Before / after">
              <button class="ba-btn on" type="button" data-show="before"><span class="lang-en">broken</span><span class="lang-ko">깨진 상태</span></button>
              <button class="ba-btn" type="button" data-show="after"><span class="lang-en">fixed</span><span class="lang-ko">고친 상태</span></button>
            </div>
            <figure class="fix-fig fig-before on">
              <div class="flow">
                <span class="fchip mem">sequential pack 0 1 2 3…</span><span class="farr">→</span>
                <span class="fchip">unpack</span><span class="farr">→</span>
                <span class="fchip warn">cross-lane shuffle at runtime</span><span class="farr">→</span>
                <span class="fchip">mma fragments</span>
              </div>
              <figcaption><span class="lang-en">before — decoded values land in the wrong lanes; fixing that costs instructions every iteration</span><span class="lang-ko">before — decode된 값이 엉뚱한 lane에 떨어지고, 매 iteration마다 instruction으로 고쳐야 한다</span></figcaption>
            </figure>
            <figure class="fix-fig fig-after">
              <div class="flow">
                <span class="fchip good">pack once, permuted: 6 4 2 0 7 5 3 1</span><span class="farr">→</span>
                <span class="fchip">lop3 unpack</span><span class="farr">→</span>
                <span class="fchip good">already in fragment layout</span>
              </div>
              <figcaption><span class="lang-en">after — the shuffle happened offline, at pack time</span><span class="lang-ko">after — shuffle은 pack 시점에 offline으로 끝났다</span></figcaption>
            </figure>
            <p class="fix-cite">
              <span class="lang-en">
                MARLIN stores weights “interleaved, according to the pattern 64207531” for parallel
                in-register decode; FLUTE reorders offline “such that after dequantization, the
                weights are already laid out exactly in the expected format”; QServe’s
                compute-aware reorder concatenates each thread’s channels “into a single 128-bit
                word” — 128-bit loads with zero runtime address math, and INT4→INT8 unpack in 3
                logic ops. KV caveat: K/V are generated at runtime, so “offline” becomes
                <em>once, at quantization time</em> — QServe’s KV page layout with inline
                scales/zeros is that instance. (Deeper cut: LUT-GEMM precomputes partial sums and
                “eliminates the resource-intensive dequantization process” entirely — 2.1× over
                the OPTQ kernel at 3-bit.)
              </span><span class="lang-ko">
                MARLIN은 weight를 “64207531 패턴으로 interleave”해 저장해 register 내 병렬
                decode를 만든다; FLUTE는 “dequantization 후 weight가 기대 format 그대로
                놓이도록” offline으로 reorder한다; QServe의 compute-aware reorder는 각 thread의
                channel을 “하나의 128-bit word로 연결” — 주소 계산 없는 128-bit load에 INT4→INT8
                unpack이 3 logic ops다. KV 주의: K/V는 runtime에 생성되므로 “offline”은
                <em>quantize 시점에 한 번</em>이 된다 — QServe의 inline scale/zero KV page
                layout이 그 사례다. (더 깊은 수: LUT-GEMM은 partial sum을 미리 계산해
                “dequantization 자체를 제거”한다 — 3-bit에서 OPTQ kernel 대비 2.1×.)
              </span>
            </p>
          </article>

          <!-- F-d LUT replication -->
          <article class="fix-card">
            <span class="card-kicker">F-d · FLUTE</span>
            <h3><span class="lang-en">LUT replication vs bank conflicts</span><span class="lang-ko">LUT 복제 vs bank conflict</span></h3>
            <div class="ba-btns" role="group" aria-label="Before / after">
              <button class="ba-btn on" type="button" data-show="before"><span class="lang-en">broken</span><span class="lang-ko">깨진 상태</span></button>
              <button class="ba-btn" type="button" data-show="after"><span class="lang-en">fixed</span><span class="lang-ko">고친 상태</span></button>
            </div>
            <figure class="fix-fig fig-before on">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 420 110" class="fig-svg" role="img" aria-label="Many lanes hitting the same shared-memory bank">
                {Array.from({ length: 8 }, (_, i) => (
                  <rect x={20 + i * 48} y="18" width="40" height="22" rx="4" fill="var(--surface-warm)" stroke="var(--line-strong)"></rect>
                ))}
                <text x="40" y="33" text-anchor="middle" class="t-mono t-tiny">bank0</text>
                {[0, 1, 2, 3, 4].map((i) => (
                  <line x1={60 + i * 70} y1="86" x2="42" y2="44" stroke="var(--accent-strong)" stroke-width="1.3"></line>
                ))}
                <text x="220" y="100" text-anchor="middle" class="t-tiny t-accent">lanes pile onto one bank → up to 8-way conflict (4-bit LUT) → 8× serialized</text>
              </svg>
              <figcaption><span class="lang-en">before — one naive table, 32 banks, colliding lanes</span><span class="lang-ko">before — 순진한 table 하나, bank 32개, 충돌하는 lane들</span></figcaption>
            </figure>
            <figure class="fix-fig fig-after">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 420 110" class="fig-svg" role="img" aria-label="Vectorized lookup table duplicated across banks">
                {Array.from({ length: 8 }, (_, i) => (
                  <g>
                    <rect x={20 + i * 48} y="18" width="40" height="22" rx="4" fill="var(--accent-soft)" stroke="var(--accent)"></rect>
                    <line x1={40 + i * 48} y1="86" x2={40 + i * 48} y2="44" stroke="var(--swatch-olive)" stroke-width="1.3"></line>
                  </g>
                ))}
                <text x="220" y="100" text-anchor="middle" class="t-tiny t-tert">vectorized LUT (all 2⁸ index pairs ≈ 1 KB), copies in different banks — conflict-free</text>
              </svg>
              <figcaption><span class="lang-en">after — pay ~1 KB of SMEM per copy, get parallel lookups</span><span class="lang-ko">after — 복사본당 SMEM ~1 KB를 내고 병렬 lookup을 얻는다</span></figcaption>
            </figure>
            <p class="fix-cite">
              <span class="lang-en">
                FLUTE documents both the problem (“up to 8-way bank conflicts” for a naive
                vectorized 4-bit table) and the fix: vectorize the LUT into all 2⁸ index-pairs and
                “duplicate the … lookup table multiple times, placing copies in different memory
                banks.” Hardware rule: 32 banks, 32 bits per bank per clock, successive words in
                successive banks; n-way conflicts serialize n× (CUDA docs). MARLIN’s non-LUT
                analogue is an XOR-swizzled SMEM layout (element (i, j) placed via i⊕j).
              </span><span class="lang-ko">
                FLUTE는 문제(“순진한 vectorized 4-bit table은 최대 8-way bank conflict”)와
                해법을 모두 기록한다: LUT를 2⁸개 index-pair 전체로 vectorize하고 “복사본을 서로
                다른 memory bank에 여러 벌” 둔다. 하드웨어 규칙: bank 32개, bank당 클럭당 32
                bit, 연속 word는 연속 bank로; n-way conflict는 n× 직렬화된다 (CUDA docs).
                MARLIN의 non-LUT 대응물은 XOR-swizzle SMEM layout이다 (element (i, j)를 i⊕j로
                배치).
              </span>
            </p>
          </article>

          <!-- F-e pipelining -->
          <article class="fix-card wide">
            <span class="card-kicker">F-e · MARLIN · (cost side: QServe on Atom)</span>
            <h3><span class="lang-en">Pipelining and the occupancy tax</span><span class="lang-ko">pipelining과 occupancy 세금</span></h3>
            <div class="ba-btns" role="group" aria-label="Before / after">
              <button class="ba-btn on" type="button" data-show="before"><span class="lang-en">broken</span><span class="lang-ko">깨진 상태</span></button>
              <button class="ba-btn" type="button" data-show="after"><span class="lang-en">fixed</span><span class="lang-ko">고친 상태</span></button>
            </div>
            <figure class="fix-fig fig-before on">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 860 96" class="fig-svg" role="img" aria-label="Serial timeline: load then compute alternating with gaps">
                {[0, 1, 2].map((i) => (
                  <g>
                    <rect x={20 + i * 280} y="24" width="130" height="24" rx="5" fill="#e6e9df" stroke="var(--swatch-olive)"></rect>
                    <text x={85 + i * 280} y="40" text-anchor="middle" class="t-mono t-tiny">load tile {i}</text>
                    <rect x={158 + i * 280} y="24" width="130" height="24" rx="5" fill="var(--accent-soft)" stroke="var(--accent)"></rect>
                    <text x={223 + i * 280} y="40" text-anchor="middle" class="t-mono t-tiny">unpack+math {i}</text>
                  </g>
                ))}
                <text x="20" y="78" class="t-tiny t-tert">serial: the math units idle during every load, the memory system idles during every unpack</text>
              </svg>
              <figcaption><span class="lang-en">before — load and compute take turns</span><span class="lang-ko">before — load와 compute가 번갈아 논다</span></figcaption>
            </figure>
            <figure class="fix-fig fig-after">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 860 120" class="fig-svg" role="img" aria-label="Pipelined timeline: four cp.async stages overlapping compute">
                {[0, 1, 2, 3].map((i) => (
                  <g>
                    <rect x={20 + i * 150} y="16" width="140" height="20" rx="5" fill="#e6e9df" stroke="var(--swatch-olive)"></rect>
                    <text x={90 + i * 150} y="30" text-anchor="middle" class="t-mono t-tiny">cp.async tile {i}</text>
                  </g>
                ))}
                {[0, 1, 2].map((i) => (
                  <g>
                    <rect x={170 + i * 150} y="44" width="140" height="20" rx="5" fill="var(--accent-soft)" stroke="var(--accent)"></rect>
                    <text x={240 + i * 150} y="58" text-anchor="middle" class="t-mono t-tiny">unpack+math {i}</text>
                  </g>
                ))}
                <text x="20" y="100" class="t-tiny t-tert">P=4 stages in flight; prefetch P−1 tiles ahead; “all shared memory addressing completely static” (MARLIN)</text>
              </svg>
              <figcaption><span class="lang-en">after — dequant hides under DRAM time … while registers last</span><span class="lang-ko">after — dequant가 DRAM 시간 밑에 숨는다 … register가 버티는 동안은</span></figcaption>
            </figure>
            <p class="fix-cite">
              <span class="lang-en">
                MARLIN runs a 4-stage cp.async pipeline with an evict_first cache hint, multiple
                warps per output tile and a logarithmic parallel reduction. The tax is registers:
                QServe observes that Atom’s dual INT32 + FP32 accumulator sets, “consuming a large
                number of registers within each warp, limit the number of warps that can be
                executed simultaneously” — occupancy loss on a 256 KB/SM register file. Deeper
                pipelines and fatter unpack sequences both spend the same budget.
              </span><span class="lang-ko">
                MARLIN은 evict_first cache hint의 4-stage cp.async pipeline, output tile당 다중
                warp, logarithmic parallel reduction으로 돈다. 세금은 register다: QServe는 Atom의
                INT32 + FP32 이중 accumulator가 “warp마다 다량의 register를 소모해 동시에 실행될
                수 있는 warp 수를 제한한다”고 지적한다 — 256 KB/SM register file 위의 occupancy
                손실. 더 깊은 pipeline과 더 살찐 unpack 시퀀스는 같은 예산을 나눠 쓴다.
              </span>
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ (f) when does it win ============ -->
    <section class="section-tight" id="crossover">
      <div class="container">
        <h2 class="viz-h">
          <span class="lang-en">f · When does it actually win?</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">f · 그래서 언제 실제로 이기는가?</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="viz-sub">
          <span class="lang-en">
            Two dials decide the regime: how many instructions each byte costs (bit-width × kernel
            quality), and whether the kernel is memory-bound at all (batch). Drag both.
          </span><span class="lang-ko">
            두 개의 다이얼이 regime을 정한다: byte 하나가 몇 개의 instruction을 요구하는가
            (bit-width × kernel 품질), 그리고 kernel이 애초에 memory-bound인가 (batch). 둘 다
            움직여 보라.
          </span>
        </p>

        <div class="cross-grid">
          <!-- left: bytes vs instructions -->
          <div class="viz-frame cross-card">
            <h3 class="cross-h"><span class="lang-en">bytes saved vs instructions added</span><span class="lang-ko">아낀 byte vs 추가된 instruction</span></h3>
            <div class="cross-controls">
              <div class="slider-row">
                <span class="slider-lbl">bits</span>
                <input type="range" id="mpk-bit-slider" min="0" max="2" step="1" value="1" aria-label="Bit width: 16, 4, or 2" />
                <span class="slider-val" id="mpk-bit-val">INT4</span>
              </div>
              <div class="mpk-modes small">
                <button class="mode-btn on" type="button" data-style="fused" id="mpk-style-fused"><span class="lang-en">fused kernel</span><span class="lang-ko">fused kernel</span></button>
